includes: Builds on the mastering metering from v10.34.37. LOUDNESS TARGET: in the Master panel pick a delivery target — Streaming (−14) · Podcast (−16) · Broadcast EBU (−23) · Cinema (−24), or none. The integrated LUFS now colours itself against it (on target within ±1 LU, red when too loud, dim when too quiet) and the true-peak turns red when it exceeds the spec ceiling (−1 dBTP, −2 for cinema). The same colour-coding shows in Tools ▸ Broadcast, so you can mix to spec before you stream. PANIC: a "Silence — all notes off" button releases every sounding note at once across the built-in poly + sub voices, any hosted AUv3 instrument and MIDI out — the standard live kill for stuck notes. All additive display/control (no audio-path change); LoudnessTarget logic is unit-tested; Xcode Compile Check green on every commit. Still honestly held for on-device verification: HaishinKit A/V streaming wiring and the master-bus AUv3 FX slot.
